CodeMirror Enhanced for DokuWiki
================================

Maintained and adapted by sebaram, based on Albert Gasset's original
CodeMirror plugin. Original copyright and GPL licensing are preserved below.
The plugin ID is codemirrorenhanced and the installation directory is
lib/plugins/codemirrorenhanced. This fork has its own extension identity.

Upstream syntax-editor documentation can be found at
http://www.dokuwiki.org/plugin:codemirror

Source code for this plugin can be found at
https://github.com/sebaram/dokuwiki-plugin-codemirror
(maintained fork of Albert Gasset's plugin).

Install a release
-----------------

Download codemirrorenhanced.tar.gz and SHA256SUMS from
https://github.com/sebaram/dokuwiki-plugin-codemirror/releases/tag/2026-10-25.3
and install the archive through DokuWiki's Extension Manager. The install
archive includes the generated dist files. GitHub's automatic source archives
require the build steps below before deployment.

For editor chat and inline AI review, also install AI Assistant 0.1.1 from
https://github.com/sebaram/dokuwiki-ai-assistant/releases/tag/v0.1.1

Migrate an existing codemirror installation
------------------------------------------

1. Keep a private backup of the old plugin folder and the wiki's root conf/.
2. Disable the old codemirror plugin in Extension Manager.
3. Install codemirrorenhanced.tar.gz and enable CodeMirror Enhanced. Check
   that it is installed at lib/plugins/codemirrorenhanced, not codemirror.
4. Verify editing, syntax colors, settings and AI chat, then uninstall the
   old codemirror plugin. Disabled-but-installed codemirror can still cause
   catalog conflict warnings on other extensions' rows.

The new plugin reads the four existing server settings from
$conf['plugin']['codemirror'] whenever the corresponding
$conf['plugin']['codemirrorenhanced'] setting has not been saved. Explicit
new settings take priority. Browser theme/keymap/editor preferences retain
their existing cm-* cookies. AI Assistant 0.1.0 needs no runtime update;
its API profiles remain in the wiki's root conf/.

If both editor plugins are enabled, the new fork waits for the old plugin
to be disabled, preventing duplicate editors. It does not change plugin
enablement, rewrite saved settings, or delete the old installation for you.

Modern DokuWiki compatibility
----------------------------

Tested on DokuWiki 2026-07-14c "Mort", PHP 8.3.6 and Chromium with the
local 61-extension compatibility mirror. CodeMirror 5 is retained so the
existing settings, themes, keymaps and DokuWiki toolbar integrations work.

The plugin supports Fastwiki AJAX editing/preview/reopen, ProseMirror
switching, native textarea-based extensions and lazy-loaded code languages.
Fastwiki's inline section buttons also survive Wiki-Style Script rebuilding
form contents, so one block can be edited without loading the whole page.
Code and file blocks can also be highlighted in page views when codesyntax
is enabled, while retaining DokuWiki's native Copy buttons. Common extension
tags and macros are colored; their individual
plugin grammars are not validated by this editor.

When dokuwiki-ai-assistant is enabled, use its toolbar button or Ctrl/Cmd+K
to work on the current selection (or the entire document with no selection).
With AI Assistant 0.1.0, conversation lives in a sidebar and suggested
additions/deletions appear directly in this editor. Accept or reject individual
change blocks or the entire proposal. Edits on the same or consecutive source
lines share one Accept/Reject control; a fully unchanged line separates blocks.
One Undo restores an accepted block. Large rewrites use one bounded replacement
block. Accepted changes use normal Undo/Redo. Proposed
text is not submitted by Preview or Save until accepted. Only an explicit Save
creates a DokuWiki revision; AI conversation does not create checkpoints.
The sidebar can use administrator-approved read-only MCP tools when enabled
for that conversation. Chat stays in memory for the open editing session.
Older AI Assistant versions retain their existing comparison-card flow.
The companion compat/aiassist-editor.patch also restores CodeMirror
selection/scroll after AI Assistant's Ctrl/Cmd+S shortcut. Apply it from
the aiassist plugin directory with patch -p1 (or install the updated editor.js
from the adjacent dokuwiki-ai-assistant repository). The patch is included
in the install archive and is already applied in the local test wiki.

Extension Manager compatibility notice
--------------------------------------

The distinct codemirrorenhanced ID does not inherit the upstream codemirror
catalog's conflict declarations or update downloads. Update this fork from
its sebaram release archive. The separate ID does not add support for other
plugins by itself.

Fastwiki full and block editing, Preview/Cancel/reopen and exact section
Save are covered by this fork's browser checks. LinkSuggest is a separate
textarea autocomplete extension; its completion dropdown is not integrated
into CodeMirror. Switch to the Native DokuWiki editor in the settings menu
when using LinkSuggest. The built-in link wizard remains available in
CodeMirror. Do not treat a catalog warning as evidence of a runtime failure,
or the tested Fastwiki integration as a claim that every listed extension
is supported.

Build and checks (Node.js 22+)
-----------------------------

    npm ci
    npm run build
    npm test
    npx grunt dist

Install the resulting codemirrorenhanced.tar.gz through Extension
Manager, or copy the release contents into lib/plugins/codemirrorenhanced. The dist
directory is generated and must be included when deploying from source.

See tests/README.md for browser checks and local extension compatibility
limits. All compatibility testing uses a disposable wiki and a mock AI API.

